Here is the root cause:
The root cause of the bug is the potential creation of multiple instances of `TableConfiguration` for the same table. If a `Tablet` holds a different instance than the one cached in the configuration maps, it will not receive updates for constraints and other configurations from ZooKeeper. This inconsistency can lead to outdated or incorrect behavior in the `Tablet`, as it relies on the configuration to manage constraints and visibility labels effectively.

